# Trivy ignore file — curated, justified CVE risk acceptances.
# Each entry MUST have a rationale. Review on every dependency bump.
# Auto-discovered by Trivy when scanning with this directory as the
# working dir (or via TRIVY_IGNOREFILE).

# ── Residual langchain-stack HIGHs ──────────────────────────────────────
# These three are fixed only in the langchain 1.x major line. The project
# is on the langchain 0.3.x line (a deliberate, tested baseline); the
# 1.x migration is tracked separately. All three are unreachable given
# how this codebase uses the libraries:

# CVE-2026-34070 — path traversal in langchain-core's legacy `load_prompt`.
# Not exploitable: prompts are built with `ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages`
# in-code; `load_prompt` is never called.
CVE-2026-34070

# CVE-2025-64439 — RCE in langgraph-checkpoint's JsonPlusSerializer "json"
# mode. Not exploitable: the pipeline compiles its graph WITHOUT a
# checkpointer, so JsonPlusSerializer is never instantiated.
CVE-2025-64439

# CVE-2026-45134 — langsmith deserializes untrusted manifests on public
# hub prompt pulls. Not exploitable: the code never pulls hub prompts;
# langsmith is used only as an optional tracing exporter.
CVE-2026-45134
